  "summary": "Traditional Libyan clothing encompasses the heritage garments worn by Libyans throughout history.",
  "description": "Traditional Libyan clothing encompasses the heritage garments worn by Libyans throughout history. These styles vary significantly based on geographical, social, and historical factors, and reflect the influences of the civilizations that have inhabited the region. Although daily use has declined in modern times, traditional attire remains highly significant during formal and social occasions as a symbol of national heritage, characterized by unique designs with roots stretching back thousands of years.\n\nAttire differs primarily between men and women, with distinct regional variations across coastal, mountainous, and desert areas. These variations are also evident among Libya's major cultural groups, including Arabs, Amazigh (Arabic: أمازيغ), Tuareg (Arabic: طوارق), and Toubou (Arabic: تبو).",
